 "note": "Verifier unanimity = all verifier labels identical (under ANLI's protocol a 3rd verifier is added only when the first 2 disagree, so this equals 'the first two agreed'). match/differ/no_majority partition each (round, class) cell by whether the writer's gold equals / differs from / lacks a strict verifier majority. P1 (structural) bets the overall writer-gold == verifier-majority rate exceeds 0.95 in EVERY round. P2 (directional, a finding either way) bets neutral is the least unanimously verified class WITHIN every round, testing whether audit 45's pooled finding is a within-round effect. P3 (directional) bets overall verifier unanimity is non-decreasing from R1 to R3 as the adversary strengthens. per_class_aggregate reproduces audit 45's per_class exactly; per_round_aggregate reproduces audit 39's per-round split. This audit measures AGREEMENT, not label correctness."
}